Practical No: 10
Title
Introduction to Deployment and Version Control for Angular Application
Aim
To prepare an Angular application for production deployment, serve the Angular build using
Express in a single deployment setup, configure environment variables for production, and
understand the basics of Git and version control.

Software Requirements
● Node.js
● Angular CLI
● Express.js
● Git
● Visual Studio Code
● Web Browser

Procedure
1. Create or use an existing Angular application.
2. Generate a production build of the Angular application using the Angular CLI.
3. Create an Express server to serve the Angular build files.
4. Configure environment variables for production settings such as API URLs.
5. Run the Express server to serve the Angular application as a single deployment.
6. Initialize a Git repository in the project folder.
7. Track project files using Git and commit changes.
8. Push the project to a remote Git repository.

Result
The Angular application was successfully prepared for production and served using an
Express server in a single deployment setup. Environment variables were configured
correctly for production use. Git was used for version control to track changes and manage
the project source code efficiently
